## Bottom line

This is NOT a change from the last 2 days, and NOT Hetzner-side. It is a pre-existing (2026-09-17) latent bug in `worker/index.ts`'s Hetzner-dedicated-IP branch that only just got triggered because VMID 142 is the **first real Hetzner dedicated-IP guest node-2 has ever actually produced**. Root cause, fully verified live: the guest's virtual NIC was wired to node-2's isolated NAT-only bridge (`vmbr1`) while being handed a real public IP/gateway that only exists on the bridge attached to the physical NIC (`vmbr0`). The two never met, so ARP for 178.63.94.111 can never resolve — explaining the guest-agent silence, SSH silence, and 100% ping loss identically on both the original PROVISION and the REINSTALL (REINSTALL just calls `provision()` again, same code path, same VM template).

## 1. Git archaeology — nothing in the 2-day window is responsible

Checked every commit `2026-09-27 00:00`–`2026-09-29 23:59` (`git log --oneline --since/--until`, ~90 commits). Filtered for actual added/removed diff lines (not just unified-diff context) containing `vmbr`, `net0`, `ipconfig0`, `allocateDedicatedIp`, `balloonFloorMB`:
```
for sha in $(git log --since="2026-09-27 00:00" --until="2026-09-29 23:59" --format=%H); do
  git show "$sha" | grep -E "^[+-]" | grep -v "^+++|^---" | grep -c "vmbr|net0|ipconfig0|allocateDedicatedIp|balloonFloorMB"
done
```
**Zero hits.** None of `worker/index.ts`, `lib/dedicated-ip.ts`, `lib/hetzner.ts`, `lib/proxmox.ts`, `lib/ipam.ts`, `lib/capacity.ts`, `lib/actions-server-lifecycle.ts` were touched at all in this window (confirmed via `git log --oneline -- <file>` per file, and by date-checking each file's actual most-recent commit — all predate 2026-09-27 by days-to-weeks).

Two commits from **2026-09-26** (just outside the window, but the most recent real touches to `provision()`) were checked in full: `48ac3786a2` and `e99660fd0f` ("Add per-server SSH management key" / "Make management-key generation best-effort"). Both only append one extra public key to the cloud-init `sshkeys` string and wrap key generation in try/catch — they never touch `net0`/`ipconfig0`/bridge logic, so they cannot explain an L2/ARP-level failure.

**Important correction to the investigation's premise:** the fleet-wide RAM/balloon-floor fix (`43ad6f772f`, "Stop squeezing paid VMs to half their RAM", dated 2026-09-28) is **NOT merged into `main` or `release/nxm-launch`** — verified with `git merge-base --is-ancestor 43ad6f772f main/origin/main/release/nxm-launch` (all return false). It only exists on the still-open branch `fix/vps-ram-allocation`. Live-confirmed on disk: `lib/capacity.ts` still has `RAM_OVERSELL_FACTOR ?? 1.5` and `worker/index.ts`'s `balloonFloorMB()` still returns `Math.max(1024, memoryMB * 0.5)` — the 50% floor. So this fix isn't deployed at all right now, and even its full diff (read in full) only touches `balloonFloorMB()`'s return value and the oversell constant — nothing network-related — so it's not a candidate cause either way.

## 2. Scope — isolated to this one VM (but structural, not a fluke)

`qm list` on node-2 shows 19 VMs. Checked `net0`/`ipconfig0` on every one:
```
